# {{Name}}

A .NET 10 game generated by Obelisk CLI, using Obelisk.Vanilla {{EngineVersion}}.

## Prerequisites

.NET 10 SDK and Windows x64 with an SDL_GPU-compatible graphics driver.
Package restore requires a NuGet source containing Obelisk.Vanilla {{EngineVersion}}
and its dependencies. Public packages are not yet published during development;
use the local feed described in the Obelisk Engine repository README.

## Build and run

```powershell
dotnet restore
dotnet build
dotnet run
```

Move the rectangle with arrow keys. Close the window to exit. Edit Game.cs to
develop your game. Open {{Name}}.csproj in Visual Studio or Rider, or this folder
in VS Code with C# support. No engine source checkout or ProjectReference is needed.

## Project layout

- Program.cs: Vanilla startup
- Game.cs: public game lifecycle and Canvas drawing
- {{Name}}.csproj: exact Obelisk.Vanilla package version
- obelisk.json: schema 1 project metadata for CLI development commands
- assets/: copied to build/publish output; project:/// asset root
- plugins/: copied local packages; install/remove while the process is stopped

Plugin rendering uses public Canvas commands. See the engine README for the local
Plugin manifest and lifecycle. CLI run/dev/build commands arrive in later stages;
use the standard dotnet commands above for this template.
